  "id": "reciprocal-altruism",
  "term": "reciprocal altruism",
  "definition": "Reciprocal altruism is a form of cooperation between individuals in which each can help the other over repeated interactions, even though there is also an opportunity to gain by not cooperating. It depends strongly on the partner’s past behavior, with individuals tending to cooperate more with those who have cooperated before.",
